"nucleus_score":0.776912,"pct_ad":0.180568,"pct_control":0.169312,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999889,"donor_log2fc":0.0759955,"donor_lfcse":0.135005,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":4.2699e-06},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"LIFR","gene_symbol_current":"LIFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000113594","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.754737,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0813155,"nucleus_score":0.680754,"pct_ad":0.392465,"pct_control":0.37931,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.986209,"donor_log2fc":0.088606,"donor_lfcse":0.147274,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.000836368},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"LIFR","gene_symbol_current":"LIFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000113594","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":3.36614e-08,"nucleus_log2fc":0.311631,"nucleus_score":5.94146,"pct_ad":0.247382,"pct_control":0.210063,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.708624,"donor_log2fc":0.208834,"donor_lfcse":0.0853998,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.043906}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000113594","module":"pink","kme":0.260954,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.683527,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000113594","entrez_id":["3977"],"uniprot":["P42702"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a protein that belongs to the type I cytokine receptor family. This protein combines with a high-affinity converter subunit, gp130, to form a receptor complex that mediates the action of the leukemia inhibitory factor, a polyfunctional cytokine that is involved in cellular differentiation, proliferation and survival in the adult and the embryo. Mutations in this gene cause Schwartz-Jampel syndrome type 2, a disease belonging to the group of the bent-bone dysplasias. A translocation that involves the promoter of this gene, t(5;8)(p13;q12) with the pleiomorphic adenoma gene 1, is associated with salivary gland pleiomorphic adenoma, a common type of benign epithelial tumor of the salivary gland. Multiple splice variants encoding two different isoforms have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Jun 2018].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P42702","text":"[Isoform 1]: Functions as a membrane-bound signal-transducing subunit either in complex with IL6ST/gp130 or as part of the ciliary neurotrophic factor receptor (CNTFR) complex composed by CNTFR, IL6ST/gp130 and LIFR (PubMed:11285233, PubMed:11294841, PubMed:1542794, PubMed:39532904, PubMed:9030543, PubMed:9188471). Signal transmission is initiated either by binding directly to cytokines, such as OSM or LIF or CTF1, or through the binding of other cytokines, like CNTF, CLCF1 or the heterodimeric complex CRLF1-CLCF1 to the non-signaling receptor CNTFR; ligand binding induces heterodimerization of IL6ST/gp130 and LIFR which activates JAK tyrosine kinases bound to their intracellular domains (PubMed:11285233, PubMed:11294841, PubMed:1542794, PubMed:1915266, PubMed:9030543, PubMed:9188471). These kinases subsequently phosphorylate the homodimer or heterodimer form of IL6ST/gp130 (PubMed:11285233, PubMed:11294841, PubMed:9030543). The tyrosine phosphorylated signaling receptors serve in turn as docking sites for recruitment and activation of signal transducer and activators of transcription (STATs) (PubMed:11285233, PubMed:11294841, PubMed:9030543, PubMed:9188471). Engages sites 3 of ligands cytokines (PubMed:36930708). [Isoform 2]: Could inhibit the biological activity of LIF by blocking its binding to receptors on target cells."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}